{ My first result against a GM, having previously lost to GM Joel Benjamin at the US Open. A draw here really validated a lot of my chess. That I had the strength to rival people at the highest level. I think I always had this issue, wondering why I'm doing something that I'm at a low level at, but this gave me a lot of strength. Now I will say this game isn't pretty, I built up and squandered an opening advantage as Black. He outplays me but misses some critical ideas to cement his advantage at a few points. And then a natural but slow move like Qc3 allows everything to trade off and I hunt down the draw. }
