s to some favorable trades and is more forcing. } { [%eval 0.01] } (11. g3 { the mainline where } 11... b6 { is my line } 12. Nf3 f6 { [%cal Gf6g5,Gf6e5] } 13. Bg2 O-O 14. O-O g5 15. c4 Ne7 16. b3 Ba6) 11... Nf5 { [%eval 0.03] } { hits the DSB immediately } { [%eval -0.01] [%csl Ge3] } (11... O-O 12. Bh6 (12. O-O) (12. Nf3!? { saves the DSB }) 12... f6 13. O-O) 12. Bf4 { [%eval -0.02] [%eval -0.04] } 12... Bxf4 { [%eval -0.08] [%eval -0.05] } 13. Nxf4 { [%eval -0.09] [%eval -0.05] } 13... Qd6 { [%eval -0.11] } { using tempos to develop quickly } { [%eval -0.02] } 14. g3 { [%eval -0.04] [%eval 0.01] } 14... Bd7 { [%eval 0.2] [%eval 0.1] } (14... f6 { may TS }) 15. Nf3 { [%eval -0.33] [%eval -0.4] } (15. O-O h5) 15... f6 { [%eval -0.32] } { getting the key structure here limiting the scope of WH's Ns } { [%eval -0.39] [%csl Gg5,Ge5][%cal Gf6g5,Gf6e5] } (15... O-O-O) 16. Qd2 { [%eval -0.32] [%eval -0.31] } (16. O-O O-O-O { and I have great attacking chances here }) 16... O-O-O { [%eval -0.28] } { leading the way } { [%eval -0.3] } 17. O-O-O { [%eval -0.31] [%eval -0.3] } (17. O-O $15 { I thought he might consider this, but yeah this looks great for BL with very easy attacking chances }) 17... g5 { [%eval -0.21] [%eval -0.12] } (17... Rhf8 { eng best, keeping things controlled before pushing for g5 }) (17... Kb8 { was worried about being slow } 18. g4 Nfe7 19. g5 { and having my structure damaged. But it actually opens things up for me too } 19... fxg5 20. Nxg5 Rdf8 { [%csl Gf2][%cal Gf8f2] } 21. Nd3 e5! { blowing everything up }) 18. Nh5 { [%eval -0.4] } { thought this was over ambitious by him, and yeah Nd3 seems slightly better } { [%eval -0.27] } (18. Nd3 e5 { was expecitng something like this } (18... Kb8)) 18... Rhf8 { [%eval -0.22] } { also good here, holding down things } { [%eval -0.26] } (18... Rdf8) (18... Qe7 { stronger to hold the pawn chain together and getting off the d file } 19. h4 h6) 19. g4 { [%eval -0.27] [%eval -0.31] } (19. h4 h6) 19... Nfe7 { [%ev